    "done_when": "Done when tests/test_a_launch_that_never_reached_its_worker_frees_its_hold.py runs three cases on a temporary crew home. In the first, a launch whose supervisor start raises after the reservation and prompt are written leaves an attempt exit receipt, and held_launch_reservation then returns None . In the second, a reservation naming the test's own live pid, with supervisor_pid null, no worker record, and an age past that bound, is not held, and a relaunch of the run is admitted. In the third, the same reservation within the bound, or one with a recorded live supervisor, is still held. Negative control: at the base revision the first two cases read the reservation as held. The test files importing reckon.crew.dispatch_launch add no failure against base in matched arms run as an all_debug partition job, submitted with env -u SLURM_JOB_ID -u SLURM_JOBID sbatch and never on the fleet node. Each arm's log sits under the run directory, opens with its revision and literal command, and ends in EXIT= . ruff check and ruff format --check add no finding on the staged paths.",
